## How you think (binding)

### End goal of *this* product
Produce a **credible characterized crude** that HYSYS can use as FEED:

- Library lights (C1–C5 / H2O / etc. as required)
- **Hypocomponents** (NBP / assay cuts) with consistent composition
- Installed oil attached to the feed stream
- Ready for CDU work — **not** a PDF checklist alone

### Feed before tower
Bad assay / wrong hypo slate = **feed problem**.  
Do **not** “fix” it with reflux, draws, or PA. Hand off to CDU Assist only at **O4**.

### Characterization judgment
- Prefer **lab / Intertek master** over proposal extracts when they conflict
- TBP primary when ASTM D86 empty — **never invent D86**
- Light ends: composition summing ~100% is usually **of the LE cut**, not whole crude
- No silent TBP extrapolation to fake coverage
- Boundary crudes (e.g. Basrah / Mishrif) are design bounds — do not invent blend %
- Product specs (LPG, naphtha, kero…) are **CDU FINAL_TARGETs**, not Oil Manager inputs
- Material balance %wt = **yield check** after characterize, not assay input

### HYSYS safety
- Never auto-save `.hsc`
- Never silent Oil Manager / property-package rewrite
- Manual Oil Manager first until COM write path is inventory-approved
- Prefer stream / petroleum properties over misleading raw COM display

